   "evidence": "`grep -n modelPdf` over `EpsilonEridani/` returns no `comap_modelPdf`/`chargeConj_modelPdf`; the only occurrence of the fact is `Meson/Pdf/Basic.lean:299-302`. `Model.lean:91-96` defines `modelPdf Flavor a b := fun _ x _ => Set.indicator ...` with `modelPdf_apply` as its only unfolding lemma, and `Basic.lean:167` defines `comap \u03c3 f := fun k => f (\u03c3 k)`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Meson/Pdf/Basic.lean",
   "fix": "Add the general lemma to `EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/Model.lean`, e.g. `@[simp] lemma comap_modelPdf {\u03b9 \u03ba : Type} (\u03c3 : \u03ba \u2192 \u03b9) (a b : \u2115) : comap \u03c3 (modelPdf \u03b9 a b) = modelPdf \u03ba a b` (the two sides are the same `fun _ x _ => Set.indicator ...`), list it in that file's key results, and replace `hshape` with it (`PDF.chargeConj` is `comap conj` by `chargeConj_eq_comap`).",
   "issue": "`chargeConj_valenceModelPdf` proves `hshape : PDF.chargeConj (PDF.modelPdf (Species Flavor) 0 1) = PDF.modelPdf (Species Flavor) 0 1` as a local `have`, by `funext` through `modelPdf_apply` twice. The statement mentions only upstream types (`Pdf`, `comap`/`chargeConj`, `modelPdf`) and depends on nothing meson-specific: it is the flavour-independence of `modelPdf`, which `Model.lean` records nowhere. Hidden this way it is unavailable to any later consumer \u2014 Layer 1.3's charge-conjugation relations among pion densities need exactly it \u2014 which would have to reprove it.",
   "line": 299
  }
 ],
